    {
      "leccion_ord": 2,
      "titulo_en": "🐱 Scratch: predict the outcome &amp; draw shapes",
      "titulo_ya_traducido": false,
      "bloques": [
        {
          "bloque_ord": 1,
          "kind": "rule",
          "html_en": "A <b>variable</b> is a named box that stores a value. In Scratch you <b>set</b> a variable to a value, and the value can change while the program runs."
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 2,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<h3>🔢 The blocks you must recognise</h3>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 4,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<h3>➖ Example: subtracting two numbers (page 60)</h3>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 5,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>when this sprite clicked</span>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 6,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>ask <span>What is the first number?</span> and wait</span>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 7,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>set <span>Number 1</span> to <span>answer</span></span>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 8,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>ask <span>What is the second number?</span> and wait</span>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 9,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>set <span>Number 2</span> to <span>answer</span></span>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 10,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>set <span>Result</span> to <span>Number 1 − Number 2</span></span>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 11,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>say <span>join Result = Result</span> for <span>2</span> seconds</span>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 12,
          "kind": "tip",
          "html_en": "Enter <b>10</b> then <b>4</b> → Sam says <b>Result = 6</b>. The variables are shown in the <b>top left</b> of the stage, and they show the value stored right now."
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 13,
          "kind": "warning",
          "html_en": "<b>Watch out:</b> when you click the <b>Green Flag</b>, the variables are <b>reset to 0</b>. That is why Section 1 contains <span>set <span>Number 3</span> to <span>0</span></span>."
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 14,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<h3>➕ Adding three numbers (page 64)</h3><p>Same idea, but with <b>three</b> ask/set pairs and <b>two</b> addition operators nested inside one <span>set Result to</span> block:</p>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 15,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>set <span>Result</span> to <span>( Number 1 + Number 2 ) + Number 3</span></span>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 16,
          "kind": "tip",
          "html_en": "To add three numbers you place <b>one addition operator inside the set block</b>, then <b>drop a second addition operator into the first blank area</b>."
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 17,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<h3>📐 Sub-routines: Draw Triangle and Draw Square (page 84)</h3><p>A <b>sub-routine</b> is your own block, made with <b>Make a block</b> in the <b>My Blocks</b> palette. You write the code once and reuse it as many times as you like.</p>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 19,
          "kind": "rule",
          "html_en": "<b>repeat = number of sides  ·  turn = 360 ÷ number of sides</b>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 21,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<h3>🎨 The Pattern algorithm</h3>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 22,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>when 🏳 clicked</span>"
        },
        {
          "bloque_ord": 23,
          "kind": "text",
          "html_en": "<span>repeat <span>3</span></span>"
        },
        {
